# Debian/Ubuntu packages that need root, installed by platform/debian/
# bootstrap.sh and checked by scripts/doctor. One name per line, # comments.
#
# Empty on purpose. Every Debian/Ubuntu machine here is a server, and a
# server's root layer (Tailscale, ssh hardening, firewall, updates) belongs
# to the fleet repository (github.com/agosmou/fleet); this repository owns
# the user layer there and installs nothing as root. The mechanism stays
# for the day the user layer itself needs a root package on a server.
#
# Same rules as the Fedora file: add here and `just sync`; remove here,
# then `sudo apt-get remove <name>` yourself.
